Startup-in-a-Box (One-Server DevOps Architecture)

A minimal, production-oriented infrastructure blueprint for small startups that need to deploy software reliably at low cost.

This project demonstrates how to provision infrastructure, containerize applications, and implement CI/CD using a single-server architecture — with a clear path to scale when needed.

🎯 Goal

Many early-stage startups need:

Low infrastructure cost

Simple deployment workflow

Basic security hardening

Reproducible infrastructure

Clear upgrade path

This project provides exactly that.

🏗 Architecture Overview

Current version (v1) uses a single cloud instance:

One virtual machine

Dockerized frontend and backend

Reverse proxy for routing

Infrastructure provisioned via Terraform

Automated deployment via CI/CD

Future versions can introduce:

Separate database server

Private subnets

Load balancer

Monitoring stack

Managed database

🛠 Tools Used

Terraform – Infrastructure provisioning

Docker – Application packaging

GitLab – Continuous Integration & Deployment

Nginx – Reverse proxy

MongoDB – Application database

📦 Infrastructure Components

VPC

Public subnet

Internet gateway

Security groups

EC2 instance

Optional RDS / external database

S3 (artifacts / backups)

🚀 Deployment Flow

Terraform provisions infrastructure.

CI pipeline builds Docker images.

Images are pushed to registry.

Server pulls latest images.

Containers restart with zero manual configuration.

🔐 Security Considerations

Database not exposed publicly

Security groups restrict traffic

Environment variables used for secrets

Reverse proxy handles public traffic

📈 Scaling Path

When scaling is required:

Move database to private subnet

Add load balancer

Add monitoring stack

Introduce configuration management

Separate staging and production environments

🎓 Purpose

This project is intended as:

A learning platform for DevOps engineering

A reproducible startup deployment template

A portfolio-ready infrastructure project


Push to main
   ↓
GitLab CI builds image
   ↓
Push to ECR
   ↓
GitLab triggers deploy step
   ↓
EC2 pulls new image
   ↓
Container restarts